== 3. Runs, final (10 Nov, after the fixes below; Verilator 5.020, every bench rebuilt from the delivered sources
       with -Wall: "[]" after "ok" means no warning)
The first run of section 3 (9 Nov, 20:28 UTC) passed every 4x4 test at seed 1 but was stopped in 3b by the
machine's time limit. Its results with the earlier test code are superseded; the problems the rest of that run and
these runs found were all in the tests or the bundle generator, none in the RTL, and are fixed:
  - BP06 failed on 2x2: every packet was injected 120 cycles before the round, a 2x2 round is 69 cycles, so packets
    left by bypass one round early. Now each source's packets are injected 30 cycles before its own turn, as many as
    one burst takes (two with B_MAX 10), so the bursts overfill the 28-flit bypass space on 2x2 too.
  - BP08 +QUICK failed at seeds 4, 7, 10 and 4000000000: no cycle of waiting packets formed in 1,000 cycles. The
    load now goes on until one forms (at most 4x); with +QUICK a cycle forming is a coverage goal (seed 4 forms none
    in 4,000 cycles), in the full form a check.
  - BP10 passed on 8x8 with the mesh saturated (0.20 packets/node/cycle > 0.137). It now runs at 0.20 on 4x4 with
    4 VCs and at the same 78% of design A's saturation elsewhere.
  - The B_MAX 5 run failed BP04's bin "packets bypassed from a mesh input": with B_MAX 5 a burst holds one packet and
    the scan's start decides where it comes from. A coverage goal for B_MAX 5 (the check stays for B_MAX >= 10).
  - make_bundle.tcl stopped: the mesh bench with its four test files is one chunk of 120,165 characters, over the
    99,000 limit. Bundles now leave out comment lines (pragmas kept): 89,266 characters for that chunk.
  - Design-B CSV rows now record b_max and t_mode (stats.sv csv_row; PERF and BP10).

